meta {
  name: A pupil who does not take the subject
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/register
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "subject_offering_id": "{{offeringId}}",
    "period_id": "{{periodOneId}}",
    "attendance_date": "2026-11-02",
    "entries": [
      {
        "student_id": "{{studentId}}",
        "status": "present"
      },
      {
        "student_id": "{{callerPersonId}}",
        "status": "absent"
      }
    ]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
  res.body.message: contains attendance_not_enrolled
  res.body.not_enrolled: isArray
}

docs {
  The refusal names the offenders in a not_enrolled array rather than just
  saying no, so a client can strike them out and resend instead of guessing
  which of forty pupils was the problem. The second id here is a person who is
  not a pupil of this class at all, which is the same shape of mistake as a
  pupil who dropped the subject.

  Enrolment must be active. A dropped subject enrolment is treated exactly
  like never having been enrolled, which is why marks stop the day a pupil
  changes elective rather than the day somebody remembers to say so.

  Nothing is written: the whole register is refused, including the pupil who
  was fine.
}
